(nearby sentence from the wrong segment if article boundaries are not perfectly isolated. The) Tj
T*
( title boost reduces this problem, but a stronger article-level document store would likely ) Tj
T*
(improve these cases further.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The largest improvement came from fixing corpus coverage. The earlier 50,000-word corpus ) Tj
T*
(truncation made the test set inconsistent with the knowledge resource because some later ) Tj
T*
(articles were absent. Keeping the full 90-article corpus improved both retrieval and ) Tj
T*
(extractive answering.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Compared with a closed-book model, the RAG system is more controllable because answers are ) Tj
T*
(drawn from collected public documents. It also avoids relying on model memory for ) Tj
T*
(publication dates, URLs, source names, and article summaries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(6. Limitations) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- The QA set is template-generated, so it is less linguistically diverse than fully human-) Tj
T*
(written questions.) Tj
T*
(- Formal inter-annotator agreement was not computed because this was completed as a single-) Tj
T*
(person project.) Tj
T*
(- The final system is optimized for article-title questions; unseen questions without exact ) Tj
T*
(article titles may require stronger semantic retrieval and reranking.) Tj
T*
(- The generated binary retrieval index is not committed to git, so it must be rebuilt with ) Tj
T*
(`scripts/build_index.py`.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(7. References) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(- Patrick Lewis et al. 2020. Retrieval-Augmented Generation for Knowledge-Intensive NLP ) Tj
T*
(Tasks.) Tj
T*
(- Rajpurkar et al. 2016. SQuAD: 100,000+ Questions for Machine Comprehension of Text.) Tj
